* Print primes up to 500 — from GNU MDK samples
* Algorithm: sieve-like, tests each odd number for divisibility
L       EQU     500         * upper bound
BUF0    EQU     2000        * output buffer base
BUF1    EQU     BUF0+25
PRIME   EQU     -1          * sentinel value
TERM    EQU     19          * output device (terminal)
        ORIG    3000
START   ENTA    1
        STA     J+3(4:4)    * adjust jump table
        ENT1    BUF1+1
        JBUS    *(TERM)
        ENTA    2
        STA     PRIME+1
2H      ENTA    3           * candidate prime
        STA     PRIME
        INC1    -1
        J1Z     DONE        * buffer full?
4H      INC2    2           * next candidate: candidate += 2
        JMP     ISPRIME
        JMP     4B          * not prime, try next
        STA     PRIME,1     * store prime
        JMP     2B
ISPRIME ENT3    1
3H      INC3    1           * check divisibility
        LD2     PRIME,3
        J2Z     ISPRIME2    * divisor = 0 → prime
        CMPX    PRIME,3
        JGE     *+2
        JMP     3B          * X < prime[3], still possible
ISPRIME2 ENT2  0
        JMP     *+1
        STJ     *+1
DONE    OUT     BUF1(TERM)
        JBUS    *(TERM)
        HLT
PRIME   ORIG    PRIME+499
        END     START
